[2026-10-05T00:20:42.324Z] [INFO]         "content": "112961:[2026-10-04T18:27:22.861Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The `.gitkeep` is a leftover from the solver's initial commit, so I'll remove it:\"\n114765:[2026-10-04T18:29:10.612Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Benchmarks and C# passed, and Rust (3 OSes) is still running. I'll compare the CI runner's speed with this machine using the size-1000 jobs:\"\n116923:[2026-10-04T18:32:32.978Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The full run (37224809082) has started. While it runs I'll check why the C# workflow is listed as \\\"csharp\\\" when its name is \\\"C#\\\":\"\n117237:[2026-10-04T18:32:37.893Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Workflows that aren't on the default branch yet are listed under their file name, so this will fix itself after the merge. I'll wait for the pull-request checks:\"\n117639:[2026-10-04T18:36:51.864Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"All PR checks pass, including Rust and C# on Windows and macOS. Next I'll check the issue and PR for new comments:\"\n118003:[2026-10-04T18:36:58.652Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"No comments yet. I'll wait for the full benchmark run in the background:\"\n118354:[2026-10-04T18:37:04.761Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"While it runs, I'll review the full diff for removed functionality:\"\n118673:[2026-10-04T18:37:09.575Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"I'll check the READMEs for links to files that no longer exist:\"\n119000:[2026-10-04T18:37:15.621Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The links are fine. I'll draft the PR description now and add the measured job durations once the run finishes. First, progress so far:\"\n119257:[2026-10-04T18:37:20.347Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Rust objects at 1M failed within two minutes. I'll download the logs:\"\n120066:[2026-10-04T18:37:39.415Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Exit code 101 means a Rust panic. I'll fetch the raw log:\"\n121720:[2026-10-04T18:38:32.303Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Locally it fails differently and within 2 seconds: `Data part should be in data memory` in `update_links`, called from our `sequence`. I'll look at how the objects stores are opened:\"\n122513:[2026-10-04T18:39:35.094Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\\n\\nSummary:\\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882.\\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\\n   - Draft PR #108 already exists. Update it with `gh pr edit` and never create a new PR.\\n   - Push only to issue-107-bce58c21006b. Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\\n   - When finishing:\\n     - Merge main if needed (currently no new main commits).\\n     - Make sure CI passes.\\n     - Check the latest issue and PR comments (none so far).\\n     - Update the PR description in the style of merged PR #106 (sections: What changed, Reproduction and regression coverage, Verification, no-UI note).\\n     - Run `gh pr ready 108`.\\n   - Put experiments in ./experiments and examples in ./examples. Git user is konard.\\n   - **Security constraint (verbatim intent):** the user's email (link.assistant.team@proton.me) may \n123842:[2026-10-04T18:39:58.898Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"I'm still tracking down the Rust objects crash at 1M. Next I'll find the smallest size that triggers it.\"\n125657:[2026-10-04T18:42:42.466Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The crash first happens at post 103,399. I'm now checking how doublets splits internal ids from external (raw) values.\"\n129033:[2026-10-04T18:44:11.468Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Upstream doublets-rs `main` still has the bug, and no issue is filed for it. I'll add a small `RawMem` wrapper in our code whose `grow` returns the whole memory. First, the trait's required methods:\"\n130418:[2026-10-04T18:44:46.811Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The fix is a small wrapper: `RawMem::grow` will delegate the growth and then return the whole memory. I'll add it as a module and use it everywhere the harness builds a store's memory.\"\n130972:[2026-10-04T18:45:32.901Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"It builds cleanly. Next I'll rerun the failing reproduction and also exercise the growth path past 2^20 for every Doublets variant.\"\n131401:[2026-10-04T18:47:39.884Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"While that runs, I'll write the regression test: a unit store and a split store created past the first growth must keep all of their links.\"\n133089:[2026-10-04T18:49:28.784Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The new test passes in 29 s with `Whole`. The earlier run already showed that the same scenario on bare `Global` aborts, so the test does reproduce the bug. Checking the background benchmark:\"\n133413:[2026-10-04T18:49:35.347Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"With the fix, objects at 200k pass for all four Doublets storages, and every checksum validates. While links at 3M runs, I'll add the README notes.\"\n133962:[2026-10-04T18:49:46.176Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"I'll turn the experiment into a minimal reproduction on plain doublets that takes a `bare|whole` argument.\"\n134582:[2026-10-04T18:50:08.854Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The reproduction confirms the exact boundary: creating link 1,040,384 panics. Now the README notes in both languages:\"\n134947:[2026-10-04T18:50:18.455Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"While links at 3M runs, I'll run the local checks the Rust CI workflow runs.\"\n135554:[2026-10-04T18:51:56.474Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"All checks pass: fmt, clippy with `-D warnings`, and 9 tests. Before pushing, I'm checking the full run, since a push to this branch queues behind it in the same concurrency group.\"\n138540:[2026-10-04T18:53:08.560Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"While the Rust jobs run, I'll draft the PR description in the style of merged PR #106.\"\n138979:[2026-10-04T18:53:17.292Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The old run's watcher finished because I canceled that run. The local links 3M check is still running. Here's the scope of the whole change against main, for the description:\"\n139316:[2026-10-04T18:53:25.713Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Main has no new commits, so no merge is needed. The local links 3M check is still running, so I'll poll it and the CI run in the foreground.\"\n139701:[2026-10-04T18:54:12.859Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Links at 3M now pass on all four Doublets storages, and the memory grows twice along the way (3M > 2^21). Polling the CI run:\"\n141389:[2026-10-04T19:04:56.229Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\\n\\nSummary:\\n1. **Primary Request and Intent**\\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791131286882.\\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\\n   - PR #108 already exists. Update it with `gh pr edit` and never create a new PR.\\n   - Push only to issue-107-bce58c21006b. Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\\n   - When finishing:\\n     - Merge main if needed (verified: main has 0 new commits).\\n     - Make sure CI passes.\\n     - Check the latest issue and PR comments.\\n     - Update the PR title and description in the style of merged PR #106 (sections: \\\"What changed\\\", \\\"Reproduction and regression coverage\\\", \\\"Verification\\\", and a closing no-UI sentence; first line \\\"Fixes #107\\\").\\n     - Run `gh pr ready 108`.\\n   - Put experiments in ./experiments. Git user is konard.\\n   - **Security constraint (verbatim intent):** the user's email (link.assista\n143110:[2026-10-04T19:15:08.590Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The Rust links 10M jobs passed in about 20 minutes each. I'm waiting on the C# 10M jobs to decide whether 100M fits in 6 hours, and meanwhile checking how many operations each step runs.\"\n144002:[2026-10-04T19:15:30.615Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"To try 100M links on CI without also starting objects jobs that can't finish in time, I'm excluding objects at 100M from the matrix as well.\"\n144384:[2026-10-04T19:15:40.731Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Holding this commit until the running benchmark run finishes, because pushing it now would start another full run. Meanwhile, I'm checking the 10M file sizes to estimate disk use at 100M.\"\n146655:[2026-10-04T19:20:39.231Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Gathering the list of changes against main for the PR description.\"\n147692:[2026-10-04T19:20:57.383Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Waiting for the C# objects jobs; the README currently says larger sizes don't fit in 6 hours, and the 100M probe will confirm or correct that.\"\n149403:[2026-10-04T19:31:22.246Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The three workflows this PR touches lint clean. The two warnings are in `AutoMerge.yml` and `cpp.yml`, which come unchanged from main.\"\n150035:[2026-10-04T19:31:54.524Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The 100M probe is queued as run 37228604862, and PR CI is running. Re-running the local checks to confirm the exact test counts for the description.\"\n150857:[2026-10-04T19:33:11.903Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Local checks all pass: Rust 9 tests, C# 28, Python 15. Now checking PR CI.\"\n151197:[2026-10-04T19:33:20.434Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"PR CI is green on 4a91975. Drafting the PR description while the C# objects 1M jobs run.\"\n151835:[2026-10-04T19:43:17.503Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"Failed to authenticate: OAuth session expired and could not be refreshed\"",
