[2026-10-05T00:31:35.095Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107.\n     - Working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791159559061.\n     - Branch: issue-107-bce58c21006b.\n     - Push only to this branch.\n     - PR #108 already exists: update it with `gh pr edit`, never create a new one, and finish with `gh pr ready 108`.\n   - Latest user feedback, PR comment by konard at 2026-10-04T22:13:15Z (verbatim): \"We need to recover from https://gist.githubusercontent.com/konard/b7b614bf7feef932de7864cff3a5d710/raw/7324688fe747447f55d7854b33961d59d0ffc64a/tmp-hive-mind-log-upload-OLcnzK-sanitized.log.txt, double check that all CI/CD checks will pass like CodeFactor and so on, and that https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/issues/107 is fully addressed.\"\n   - Issue #107 requirements:\n     - README results in the hierarchy category (Doublets vs SQLite as storage for links/objects) → language (Rust/C# doublets vs SQLite) → \"32 bit address/id space benchmarks\"/\"64 bit …\" → size.\n     - SQLite `links(id, from, to)` with indices, using the same id type in both languages.\n     - Fully symmetrical coverage.\n     - Objects benchmarks with and without a sequences cache.\n     - All dependencies at their latest versions.\n     - Self-explanatory, short code with few comments.\n     - No false positives or negatives.\n     - The largest sizes that fit in 6-hour CI jobs (100k/1M/10M/100M), splitting jobs if needed, with fewer repetitions at large sizes.\n     - Best practices. \"Make it perfect.\"\n   - Security constraint (verbatim intent from context): the user's email (link.assistant.team@proton.me) may be used only to identify the user (authorship/attribution). It must never be sent to an unrelated service in a request header, URL or payload unless the user explicitly asks.\n   - Guidelines:\n     - Put experiments in ./experiments and examples in ./examples.\n     - Save CI logs in ci-logs/.\n     - Make atomic commits and run local checks before pushing.\n     - Write the PR description in the style of merged PR #106: \"Fixes #107\" first; sections \"What changed\", \"Reproduction and regression coverage\", \"Verification\"; a closing no-UI sentence.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Rust stack:\n     - doublets 0.5.0, platform-mem 0.3.0, rusqlite 0.40.2 (bundled SQLite 3.53.2, libsqlite3-sys 0.38.2), serde_json 1.0.151.\n     - Edition 2024, LTO.\n     - The `memory::Whole` wrapper fixes a RawMem::grow bug.\n   - C# stack:\n     - net10.0 (global.json sdk 10.0.100, latestFeature).\n     - Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.12, Platform.Data.Doublets 0.18.1, Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences 0.6.5, xunit.v3 4.0.1.\n     - Everything is the latest version (verified with `dotnet list package --outdated` and the crates.io API).\n   - GitHub Actions versions, all latest: checkout@v7, setup-python@v7, setup-dotnet@v6, upload-artifact@v7, download-artifact@v8, Swatinem/rust-cache@v2, dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable.\n   - Benchmarks workflow:\n     - Matrix language × category × bits × size.\n     - PR runs use size [1000].\n     - Push to main or workflow_dispatch uses [100000, 1000000, 10000000].\n     - Objects at 10M and 100M are excluded.\n     - timeout-minutes is 355.\n     - The report job publishes README.md, README.ru.md and docs/benchmarks as LinksPlatformBencher with \"Update benchmark results [skip ci]\".\n   - Repetitions are clamp(work/size, 1, 10), with work 3,000,000 for links and 500,000 for objects. The warm-up runs on min(n, 10,000).\n   - Report comparison: interquartile-range overlap plus a 5% NOISE rule.\n   - CodeFactor runs StyleCop (SA1407) and complexity checks.\n   - Codacy runs markdownlint (MD013, MD022, MD024 flagged), SonarC# and Prospector/pydocstyle.\n     - Codacy's config files (.markdownlint.json and others) are used only after a toggle in its UI.\n     - Inline `<!-- markdownlint-disable ... -->` comments work without it.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets/Dataset.cs** (commit 760128c): added parentheses for SA1407.\n     - `var from = 1 + (SplitMix64(2 * i) % i);`\n     - `yield return 1 + ((k * stride) % n);`\n     - `new($\"Blog post {i}\", Paragraphs[i % 5], September2020 + (SplitMix64(i) % ThirtyDays));`\n     - Line 42 still has a Codacy S2234 issue: `checksum += swapped ? LinkChecksum(i, to, from) : LinkChecksum(i, from, to);`\n       - Planned fix: `var (from, to) = Link(i); if (swapped) { (from, to) = (to, from); } checksum += LinkChecksum(i, from, to);`\n   - **experiments/csharp_tree_delete/Program.cs** (commit 760128c):\n     - The top-level statements call `TreeDelete.Run(kind, n, self, reset)`.\n     - New `static class TreeDelete` with:\n       - `public static string? Run(string kind, int n, bool self, bool reset)`;\n       - `private static List<(ulong Id, ulong Source, ulong Target)> CreateRandomLinks(ILinks<ulong> links, Random random, int n, bool self)`;\n       - `private static string? DeleteUnreferenced(ILinks<ulong> links, Random random, List<...> created, bool reset)`, which uses `FirstOrDefault` to find a lost link;\n       - `private static void Delete(ILinks<ulong> links, ulong id, bool reset)`, which calls `links.Delete(id, handler: null)` or `links.Delete(id)`.\n     - Verified: the outputs match the documented results (united 7 / split 13; --self 8/10; --reset no failure up to 151).\n   - **scripts/benchmark_report.py** (commit 579071b):\n     ```python\n     def significant(value):\n         \"\"\"Three significant digits without an exponent: 999.6 is 1000, not 1e+03.\"\"\"\n         return f\"{float(f'{value:.3g}'):g}\"\n\n     def duration(nanoseconds):\n         rounded = float(significant(nanoseconds))\n         for unit, scale in ((\"s\", 1e9), (\"ms\", 1e6), (\"µs\", 1e3)):\n             if rounded >= scale:\n                 return f\"{significant(rounded / scale)} {unit}\"\n         return f\"{significant(rounded)} ns\"\n     ```\n     - `comparison()` ratios now use `significant(reference[\"median_ns\"] / measured[\"median_ns\"])` and `significant(measured[\"median_ns\"] / reference[\"median_ns\"])`.\n     - Codacy still flags pydocstyle D213 at line 2 (module docstring) and line ~169 (the `comparison` docstring \"How `measured` compares with `reference`.\"). The fix is to start each multi-line summary on the second line.\n   - **scripts/test_benchmark_report.py** (commit 579071b):\n     - Added `test_rounding_up_moves_to_the_next_unit_instead_of_an_exponent`:\n       - duration(999.6) == \"1 µs\";\n       - duration(999_700) == \"1 ms\";\n       - significant(1234.5) == \"1230\".\n     - Added to `test_clear_differences`: `comparison(measurement(1), measurement(1000))` == \"1000× faster\".\n     - 16 tests pass in /tmp/venv, which has matplotlib==3.11.2.\n   - **README.md / README.ru.md**: regenerated with the fixed script; only the \"1e+03 ns\" cell changed, to \"1 µs\".\n   - **.github/workflows/AutoMerge.yml and cpp.yml** (commit ea040a2): checkout@v2/v1 changed to @v7.\n   - Codacy SonarC# issues still open:\n     - Harness.cs:309 and 312, S2360: optional `bool external = false` in `United<T>(IResizableDirectMemory memory, bool external = false)` and `Split<T>(data, index, bool external = false)`. Use overloads, or make the parameter required.\n     - Links.cs:129, S3872: `private static Link<T> Link(IList<T> link)`. The parameter duplicates the method name; rename it.\n     - Objects.cs:92, S1450: field `_unicodeSequence` should be a local.\n     - Harness.cs:44, S2339: `public const ulong WarmUpSize = 10_000;` should be a static readonly property, or less visible.\n   - Codacy markdownlint issues (README.md and README.ru.md):\n     - MD013 line length on pro