[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-[![Rust](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/rust.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/rust.yml) [![C#](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/csharp.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/csharp.yml) [![Benchmarks](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/benchmarks.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/benchmarks.yml)",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " # Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets ([русская версия](README.ru.md))",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+[![Rust](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/rust.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/rust.yml)",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+[![C#](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/csharp.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/csharp.yml)",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+[![Benchmarks](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/benchmarks.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets/actions/workflows/benchmarks.yml)",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ![Comparison of models](https://github.com/LinksPlatform/Documentation/raw/master/doc/ModelsComparison/relational_model_vs_associative_model_vs_links.png)",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-Comparison of SQLite and LinksPlatform's Doublets (links) on basic embedded database operations with links and object-like structures.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+Comparison of SQLite and LinksPlatform's Doublets (links) on basic embedded",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+database operations with links and object-like structures.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-Based on examples from https://github.com/FahaoTang/dotnetcore-examples and https://github.com/Konard/LinksPlatform",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+Based on examples from <https://github.com/FahaoTang/dotnetcore-examples> and",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+<https://github.com/Konard/LinksPlatform>",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ## Benchmarks",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-Rust ([doublets](https://crates.io/crates/doublets) and [rusqlite](https://crates.io/crates/rusqlite) with bundled SQLite) and C# ([Platform.Data.Doublets](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Platform.Data.Doublets), [Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences) and [Microsoft.Data.Sqlite](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Microsoft.Data.Sqlite)) run the same workloads on the same deterministic data, with 32 bit (`u32`/`uint`) and 64 bit (`u64`/`ulong`) ids:",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+Rust ([doublets](https://crates.io/crates/doublets) and",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+[rusqlite](https://crates.io/crates/rusqlite) with bundled SQLite) and C#",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+([Platform.Data.Doublets](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Platform.Data.Doublets),",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+[Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences)",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+and [Microsoft.Data.Sqlite](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Microsoft.Data.Sqlite))",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+run the same workloads on the same deterministic data, with 32 bit",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+(`u32`/`uint`) and 64 bit (`u64`/`ulong`) ids:",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-- **Links**: SQLite stores the table `links(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, \"from\", \"to\")` with the indices `(\"from\", \"to\")` and `(\"to\", \"from\")`; Doublets stores the links themselves. The operations are create, read all, read by id, search by `(from, to)`, read by `from`, read by `to`, update (swap `from` and `to`) and delete.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-- **Objects**: blog posts with a title, content and publication date. SQLite stores the table `blog_posts(id, title, content, publication_date)`; Doublets stores every post as links, with strings as sequences of Unicode symbols, like [Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences](https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets.Sequences) does. The operations are create, read all, read by id and delete. Every Doublets store runs with and without a cache of the string sequences (`Cached`/`Uncached`).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+- **Links**: SQLite stores the table",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  `links(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, \"from\", \"to\")` with the indices",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  `(\"from\", \"to\")` and `(\"to\", \"from\")`; Doublets stores the links themselves.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  The operations are create, read all, read by id, search by `(from, to)`,",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  read by `from`, read by `to`, update (swap `from` and `to`) and delete.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+- **Objects**: blog posts with a title, content and publication date. SQLite",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  stores the table `blog_posts(id, title, content, publication_date)`;",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  Doublets stores every post as links, with strings as sequences of Unicode",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  symbols, like",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  [Platform.Data.Doublets.Sequences](https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets.Sequences)",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  does. The operations are create, read all, read by id and delete. Every",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  Doublets store runs with and without a cache of the string sequences",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  (`Cached`/`Uncached`).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-Storages: SQLite in memory and in a file; Doublets united (one array of links with index trees) and split (separate data and index arrays), each volatile (in memory) and non-volatile (in memory-mapped files). Doublets are compared with SQLite of the same durability: volatile with `SQLite Memory`, non-volatile with `SQLite File`.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+Storages: SQLite in memory and in a file; Doublets united (one array of links",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+with index trees) and split (separate data and index arrays), each volatile",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+(in memory) and non-volatile (in memory-mapped files). Doublets are compared",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+with SQLite of the same durability: volatile with `SQLite Memory`,",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+non-volatile with `SQLite File`.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-Every repetition runs on a fresh store in an empty directory, after one discarded warm-up repetition on up to 10,000 records. Each operation is one timed transaction over all records, point operations visit the records in a scattered order, and each result is checked against the expected count and order-sensitive checksum, so a storage that loses, duplicates or mixes up records fails the run instead of being reported as fast. Repetitions are `3,000,000 / size` for links and `500,000 / size` for objects, clamped to `1..=10`. The tables show the median time per operation; a difference is reported only if the interquartile ranges (the middle half) of the repetitions do not overlap and the medians differ by more than 5%, otherwise it is `≈ same`. The file size is measured after creation; Doublets files are preallocated memory-mapped files, so small stores show the preallocation size.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+Every repetition runs on a fresh store in an empty directory, after one",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+discarded warm-up repetition on up to 10,000 records. Each operation is one",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+timed transaction over all records, point operations visit the records in a",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+scattered order, and each result is checked against the expected count and",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+order-sensitive checksum, so a storage that loses, duplicates or mixes up",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+records fails the run instead of being reported as fast. Repetitions are",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+`3,000,000 / size` for links and `500,000 / size` for objects, clamped to",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+`1..=10`. The tables show the median time per operation; a difference is",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+reported only if the interquartile ranges (the middle half) of the",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+repetitions do not overlap and the medians differ by more than 5%, otherwise",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+it is `≈ same`. The file size is measured after creation; Doublets files are",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+preallocated memory-mapped files, so small stores show the preallocation size.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-Every table is measured by its own GitHub Actions job, with all variants on the same runner, by the [Benchmarks workflow](.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml): links with 100,000, 1,000,000 and 10,000,000 records and objects with 100,000 and 1,000,000 records (larger sizes do not fit into the 6 hour limit of a job). Pull requests check the whole pipeline on 1,000 records, and pushes to `main` update the results below. The workflow can also be started manually with other sizes.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+Every table is measured by its own GitHub Actions job, with all variants on",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+the same runner, by the [Benchmarks workflow](.github/workflows/benchmarks.yml):",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+links with 100,000, 1,000,000 and 10,000,000 records and objects with 100,000",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+and 1,000,000 records (larger sizes do not fit into the 6 hour limit of a",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+job). Pull requests check the whole pipeline on 1,000 records, and pushes to",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+`main` update the results below. The workflow can also be started manually",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+with other sizes.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " Run locally:",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ```bash",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " mkdir -p results",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-cargo run --release --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -- links 64 100000 --output results/links-rust-64-100000.json",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-dotnet run -c Release --project csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets -- objects 32 1000 --variants SQLite_File,Doublets_Split_NonVolatile_Cached",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-python3 scripts/benchmark_report.py results  # prints the tables, add --readme README.md --charts docs/benchmarks to update this file",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+cargo run --release --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -- \\",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  links 64 100000 --output results/links-rust-64-100000.json",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+dotnet run -c Release --project csharp/SQLiteVSDoublets -- \\",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  objects 32 1000 --variants SQLite_File,Doublets_Split_NonVolatile_Cached",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+# print the tables, add --readme README.md --charts docs/benchmarks to update",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+python3 scripts/benchmark_report.py results",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ```",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " Notes:",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-- The split stores of doublets 0.5.0 (Rust) lose a link that is updated to reference itself, so the benchmark updates a link to `(0, 0)` first, which is the state links are created in ([experiments/split_store_delete](experiments/split_store_delete)).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-- The stores of doublets 0.5.0 (Rust) take the part of the memory that `platform-mem` 0.3.0 returns after growing it for the whole memory, so a store fails after 1,040,384 links; the benchmarks wrap the memory in [`memory::Whole`](rust/src/memory.rs), which returns the whole memory ([experiments/unit_store_growth](experiments/unit_store_growth)).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-- In C#, links are deleted with `Delete(id, handler: null)`, which resets the link before deleting it; the bare `Delete(id)` leaves the link in the index trees, and later searches fail ([experiments/csharp_tree_delete](experiments/csharp_tree_delete)).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-- The C# united stores use AVL index trees: the default size balanced trees degenerate when many links share a source or a target, which makes each blog post creation linear in the number of posts ([experiments/csharp_objects_profile](experiments/csharp_objects_profile)).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-- Objects stores use external references for numbers and Unicode symbols, so raw values never collide with link ids.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "-- Reading a string without the cache walks its sequence link by link; in C# each `GetSource`/`GetTarget` call of `Platform.Data` allocates a handler and a list, which makes the uncached C# reads much slower than the Rust ones.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+- The split stores of doublets 0.5.0 (Rust) lose a link that is updated to",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  reference itself, so the benchmark updates a link to `(0, 0)` first, which",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  is the state links are created in",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  ([experiments/split_store_delete](experiments/split_store_delete)).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+- The stores of doublets 0.5.0 (Rust) take the part of the memory that",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  `platform-mem` 0.3.0 returns after growing it for the whole memory, so a",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  store fails after 1,040,384 links; the benchmarks wrap the memory in",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  [`memory::Whole`](rust/src/memory.rs), which returns the whole memory",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  ([experiments/unit_store_growth](experiments/unit_store_growth)).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+- In C#, links are deleted with `Delete(id, handler: null)`, which resets the",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  link before deleting it; the bare `Delete(id)` leaves the link in the index",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  trees, and later searches fail",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  ([experiments/csharp_tree_delete](experiments/csharp_tree_delete)).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+- The C# united stores use AVL index trees: the default size balanced trees",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  degenerate when many links share a source or a target, which makes each",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  blog post creation linear in the number of posts",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  ([experiments/csharp_objects_profile](experiments/csharp_objects_profile)).",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+- Objects stores use external references for numbers and Unicode symbols, so",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  raw values never collide with link ids.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+- Reading a string without the cache walks its sequence link by link; in C#",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  each `GetSource`/`GetTarget` call of `Platform.Data` allocates a handler and",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 "+  a list, which makes the uncached C# reads much slower than the Rust ones.",
[2026-10-05T00:32:38.328Z] [INFO]                 " ",
